# bix-43-q5 — CBD/cisplatin combination: DEGs + enrichment attempt (final report)

Question: *primary cellular mechanism enriched in the CBD/cisplatin combination treatment with
gseapy + Reactome_2022 on all DEGs (p<0.05, |lfc|>0.5, baseMean>10)?*

Executed code: `analysis/run_full_pipeline.py` (end-to-end, 200 s, log `results/run_full_log.txt`),
modules `analysis/deseq_np.py` (DESeq2-equivalent NB GLM), `analysis/ora.py` (gseapy-equivalent ORA),
`analysis/run_enrichment.py`, `analysis/run_marker_diagnostic.py`, validation scripts
`analysis/_validate_core.py`, `analysis/_validate_wald.py`, `analysis/_validate_ora.py`.

## 0. Method + validation
* DESeq2-equivalent NB GLM (median-of-ratios size factors, closed-form group-mean betas, MLE
  NB2 dispersion + local trend + MAP shrinkage, Wald test). R/DESeq2, pydeseq2, gseapy are all
  absent and the runner has NO network (`pip install gseapy` -> DNS failure; TCP to 8.8.8.8 ->
  "Network is unreachable"), so the algorithm was re-implemented and validated:
  - NB log-likelihood identical to `scipy.stats.nbinom` (max abs diff 6.2e-11);
  - analytic dispersion score = finite difference (rel. err 5e-4); dispersion MLE = scipy
    bounded optimiser (0/30 mismatches);
  - betas / SE / Wald p on REAL data identical to an independently written NB likelihood refit
    (max |Δlog2FC| 1.4e-2, max |ΔSE| 1.1e-3; p agrees except where p is astronomically small);
  - ORA p-values identical to `scipy.stats.fisher_exact` (alternative='greater'), BH verified,
    planted-signal recovery test passed.
* Documented deviations from R/DESeq2: binned-median dispersion trend instead of the parametric
  `a1+a2/mu` fit; single prior width 0.2; no Cook's-distance outlier replacement; no independent
  filtering (per brief). Borderline genes may therefore shift slightly.

